Warmup keyword matching
------------------------
- Filtered the 55 named-rotation posts to ones with state=PUBLISHED (i.e.
  actually live, not just queued) and a caption/topic matching Warmup
  keywords (breath, buzz, breathing exercise, resistance on the breath,
  isolating the instrument as a warmup drill) per the pillar's keyword set.
- Found roughly 10 published items touching breath/warmup in some way.
  Excluded:
    * A same-caption duplicate-topic risk: "Vocal Technique & Breath — with
      Adri" appears twice (2026-08-20 and 2026-08-21, two DIFFERENT YouTube
      video IDs but identical caption text) — used only ONE of the two to
      avoid a near-duplicate-reading pair of blog posts.
    * "Breathing Exercise for Performance — with Ashley" (2026-08-29) and
      several other 2026-08-29 posts used a bare "More at omegabone.com"
      with no /VocalMastery or /Learn2Sing path. Per SKILL.md's caption
      conventions, bare omegabone.com (no path) is the Frequency brand's
      convention specifically, and Frequency has no footage yet — so this
      was ambiguous whether it's actually VME/L2S content with a caption
      typo/format change, or something else. Rather than guess the brand
      wrong (SKILL.md flags this as a costly mistake made before, on
      2026-08-22), I skipped these and used only clips with an explicit
      /VocalMastery or /Learn2Sing path so the internal link in each blog
      post is unambiguous. This did not block the run — 7 good matches
      remained without touching the ambiguous batch.
    * Several other published named-rotation clips were excluded as
      off-topic for Warmup specifically (fear of singing, mouth shape/
      vowels = Diction, getting a good coach, welcome/intro clips, being
      emotional = Emotional Delivery, multitasking while performing =
      The Stage) — reserving those for their matching future pillar weeks.

