verbatim ("post 3 = soft CTA, post 5 = strong CTA, posts 1/2/4/6/7 = no
explicit CTA"). Note: taken as a standalone rule, post #6 is also divisible
by 3 and would read as "soft" under the general /3-/5 rule described just
above that line — but the task gave an explicit, unambiguous list for
tonight's 7 posts specifically, the same way it gave the pillar directly
rather than asking me to compute it. Followed the explicit list as the
authoritative instruction for tonight rather than re-deriving it, so post
#6 has no explicit CTA, matching what's written in its file.

Each post embeds/links its source clip's live YouTube URL and includes a
natural internal link to omegabone.com/VocalMastery (VME clips) or
omegabone.com/Learn2Sing (the one L2S clip, Upanisha's "Breath Management").
No hashtags, no emoji, per established caption/voice conventions. No hard
sell of "Frequency" except in the two CTA-tier posts (soft on #3, strong on
#5), consistent with "posts illustrate, they do not teach" and "don't
hard-sell in every post."

